{"type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [{"id": "0", "type": "Feature", "properties": {"id": "0", "name": "Colorado West Slope / Colorado River Basin (CO)", "areasqkm": 131086.6, "source": "USGS WBD HUC-8 set (HUC-4 1401,1402,1403,1405,1408), dissolved", "pulldate": "2026-07-28", "srcurl": "https://hydro.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/wbd/MapServer/4", "caveat": "Dissolved union of 30 HUC-8 subbasins making up Colorado's West Slope portion of the Colorado River watershed (HUC-4 1401,1402,1403,1405,1408). Used as the basin-scale reference boundary for statewide orgs. Cleaned 7/29/26: the dissolve of 30 HUC-8 subbasins left 422 tiny interior holes (up to 1.7 km2 down to nothing) where adjacent subwatersheds did not perfectly seal at shared edges - these rendered as small isolated navy-outlined gap shapes scattered across the basin (visible e.g. near Kremmling). Dropped all interior holes and kept just the exterior boundary, since a real watershed has no legitimate internal exclaves."}, "geometry": {"type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [[[-108.2565, 36.4823], [-108.263, 36.485], [-108.2654, 36.4978], [-108.2572, 36.5051], [-108.2714, 36.5175], [-108.2695, 36.5245], [-108.281, 36.5397], [-108.2843, 36.5561], [-108.332, 36.5781], [-108.3362, 36.5876], [-108.3606, 36.604], [-108.3661, 36.6186], [-108.3801, 36.6167], [-108.3752, 36.6237], [-108.3837, 36.6335], [-108.4065, 36.6399], [-108.4139, 36.6592], [-108.4363, 36.681], [-108.4305, 36.6983], [-108.4441, 36.7075], [-108.4503, 36.7235], [-108.4916, 36.7102], [-108.5019, 36.7275], [-108.5177, 36.7234], [-108.5696, 36.7289], [-108.6217, 36.7515], [-108.6415, 36.7741], [-108.6486, 36.7719], [-108.6468, 36.7529], [-108.6715, 36.7339], [-108.7105, 36.6854], [-108.7318, 36.6778], [-108.7719, 36.6809], [-108.7865, 36.6886], [-108.8142, 36.6546], [-108.8387, 36.6565], [-108.846, 36.649], [-108.8366, 36.6321], [-108.8485, 36.6119], [-108.8425, 36.6043], [-108.8582, 36.5821], [-108.8856, 36.5765], [-108.891, 36.5683], [-108.9